# TypeScript testing

## Runner

This project uses **Vitest** (`npm test`, `npm run test:watch`).

## TDD (Matt `/tdd`)

- Test at **pre-agreed seams** only — confirm seams before writing tests
- Red → green → next slice (vertical, not horizontal)
- Tests describe user-visible behaviour through public interfaces
- No implementation-coupled tests (mocking internals, asserting private state)

## File layout

- Co-locate domain tests: `src/lib/<domain>/<module>.test.ts`
- Mirror the module under test; one concern per test file when possible

## Assertions

- Expected values from independent sources (spec, worked example) — not recomputed like the code
- Prefer pure function tests for domain modules
- Run single test files during development; full suite before claiming done

## Coverage

No fixed percentage gate. Cover seams and critical paths agreed in the ticket/PRD.
